                    sum_r3_weak:            `Integration depth off the calibrated point.`,
                    sum_r4_good:            `Agile under the shock; honest bridge to the board.`,
                    sum_r4_weak:            `Froze or defended the price under the shock.`,

                    insight_disciplined:    `A disciplined deal: synergy cleared the €12M floor, the engineers stayed, the ARR was saved, and the NPV is positive. You bought a capability you could actually integrate — and you proved the value rather than asserting it. This is Gomes's thesis vindicated: the integration process and the people, not the price, made the deal.`,
                    insight_floor:          `You missed the €12M run-rate synergy floor. The board's clawback condition triggers and the strategy is reopened. Whatever the strategic logic, the deal failed the one test the board set — and synergy you can't deliver is synergy you never had.`,
                    insight_value:          `You cleared the floor but the NPV is negative: the value created was eaten by the control premium, the integration spend, or the talent you lost. Closing a deal and creating value are not the same thing.`,
                    insight_fragile:        `You scraped over the line, but the deal is fragile: a thin margin above the floor, with talent or board confidence that could still tip it. The lesson held only just.`,
                    insight_cliff:          `You chose to build, and the module shipped past the renewal cliff. The three at-risk customers — €16M of ARR — renewed with the rival before you were ready. Speed to the cliff was the whole point, and control cost you the customers control was meant to protect.`,
                    insight_curse:          `You paid a control premium against synergy you over-promised. The winner's curse is precise: the price was justified by value that was never real, and the gap showed up exactly where the board looks — the NPV.`,
                    insight_talent:         `More than half the acquired engineers walked. The value you bought was the talent, and you integrated it out the door. No retention plan survives contact with a six-month forced absorption.`,
                    insight_overintegrate:  `You absorbed the target fast to hit the synergy target — and triggered the 30–50% engineer flight that destroyed it. The synergy you captured was from people who'd already quit. This is the central PMI trap, in numbers.`,
                    insight_overpreserve:   `You ring-fenced the target to protect its culture and left no mechanism to capture synergy at all. You preserved a happy, disconnected subsidiary — and forfeited the €12M the board funded the move to create.`,
                    insight_arr:            `You did not save the full €16M of at-risk ARR. The capability arrived too late or too partially to hold all three renewal-conditional customers — and lost ARR is value that never reaches the synergy line.`,

                    hint_cliff:             `Build ships in 20–24 months; the cliff is ~12. The €16M of at-risk ARR renews before you're ready — speed to the cliff has to dominate the mode choice.`,
                    hint_curse:             `You're carrying an overpaid premium. The price rests on synergy you over-promised; a disciplined bridge or a structured (earn-out) price would have protected the NPV.`,
                    hint_talent:            `The engineers are leaving and they ARE the asset. Pull back on integration depth and timeline, and put a real retention + autonomy plan behind the joint pod.`,
                    hint_absorb:            `Full fast absorption is exactly when 30–50% of acquired engineers leave. Dial depth back toward the calibrated middle and capture synergy through a joint pod, not a forced migration.`,
                    hint_ringfence:         `A fully standalone unit has no mechanism to combine the module or cross-sell it. Find the minimum integration that captures synergy without breaking the culture.`,
                    hint_strong:            `You've cleared the floor and held the talent. Hold your discipline through the shock — agility under the Round-4 event is what locks the value in.`,

